1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,829
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:05,760
In this lesson, we will make
alerts reach the intended audience.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:11,089
Repeated messages create noise, while
incomplete contacts and device preferences

4
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:13,619
can leave intended recipients unreachable.

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:17,470
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,589
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:20,389 --> 00:00:24,759
An administrator creates notification
rules for new calls, builds an

8
00:00:24,769 --> 00:00:29,490
officer's distribution list, then runs
a communication test before going live.

9
00:00:29,679 --> 00:00:32,430
A dispatch only helps
if it reaches people.

10
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:36,259
This is where you confirm members
can actually be contacted.

11
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:40,379
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:42,829
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:43,649 --> 00:00:47,790
Notification rules, rules that
alert chosen people when calls,

14
00:00:48,029 --> 00:00:50,120
statuses, or other events happen.

15
00:00:50,309 --> 00:00:53,479
Create notification rules
for the events officers and

16
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,590
administrators need to know about.

17
00:00:56,349 --> 00:01:01,509
Distribution lists, reusable recipient
lists, including email lists.

18
00:01:01,919 --> 00:01:05,809
Create lists for groups you
message often, such as officers.

19
00:01:06,619 --> 00:01:11,579
Communication tests, test messages that
show whether members can be reached.

20
00:01:11,739 --> 00:01:16,069
Run a communication test before
going live and after major changes.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,949
Chat, team chat for members.

22
00:01:19,169 --> 00:01:22,229
Create channels for your
teams once chat is enabled.

23
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:25,330
Inbox, messages sent to you.

24
00:01:25,489 --> 00:01:28,899
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

25
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,749
and installed the Responder app.

26
00:01:30,939 --> 00:01:33,600
Availability also depends on messaging.

27
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:36,039
Check access in the target department.

28
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:39,550
Sent messages, messages you have sent.

29
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:43,130
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

30
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:44,959
and installed the Responder app.

31
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:47,819
Availability also depends on messaging.

32
00:01:48,019 --> 00:01:50,269
Check access in the target department.

33
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:55,629
New message, send a message, poll,
or callback request to members.

34
00:01:55,829 --> 00:01:59,239
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

35
00:01:59,239 --> 00:02:01,069
and installed the Responder app.

36
00:02:01,279 --> 00:02:03,939
Availability also depends on messaging.

37
00:02:04,139 --> 00:02:06,369
Check access in the target department.

38
00:02:07,159 --> 00:02:11,759
Chatbot and assistant integration
settings, connect the ResGrid assistant to

39
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:14,240
chat platforms and choose what it may do.

40
00:02:14,399 --> 00:02:17,809
Make sure members have added a
mobile number or email address

41
00:02:17,809 --> 00:02:19,629
and installed the Responder app.

42
00:02:20,492 --> 00:02:25,531
Account linking associates a member with
a configured external assistant platform.

43
00:02:25,762 --> 00:02:30,792
Confirm a platform is configured,
generate a short-lived linking code, and

44
00:02:30,792 --> 00:02:33,381
complete linking in the intended platform.

45
00:02:33,542 --> 00:02:37,001
Review the linked identity and
a controlled permitted action.

46
00:02:37,212 --> 00:02:39,911
Keep the temporary code
out of the recording.

47
00:02:40,132 --> 00:02:43,131
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

48
00:02:43,132 --> 00:02:44,791
recording the live workflow.

49
00:02:45,622 --> 00:02:48,521
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

50
00:02:48,721 --> 00:02:53,191
Step one: confirm member contacts
and notification preferences.

51
00:02:53,441 --> 00:02:58,872
Step two: create an officer's distribution
list and a focused notification rule.

52
00:02:59,061 --> 00:03:04,431
Step three: run an explicit communication
test and review the recorded outcomes.

53
00:03:05,261 --> 00:03:06,902
Now verify the result.

54
00:03:07,131 --> 00:03:11,512
Ask test recipients to confirm the
actual channel and time received.

55
00:03:11,671 --> 00:03:14,892
Review missing or failed results
and the intended audience.

56
00:03:15,122 --> 00:03:19,601
A common problem to watch for: a
provider handoff is not confirmed

57
00:03:19,601 --> 00:03:25,291
delivery, staffing suppression, recipient
selection, and contact eligibility

58
00:03:25,292 --> 00:03:26,951
each deserve a separate check.

59
00:03:27,752 --> 00:03:29,591
Your practice task is simple.

60
00:03:29,801 --> 00:03:31,822
Send only to the demo audience.

61
00:03:32,011 --> 00:03:37,491
Record recipients, observed receipts,
failures, and follow-up actions.

62
00:03:37,701 --> 00:03:39,811
Compare with the expected audience.

63
00:03:40,021 --> 00:03:44,541
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

64
00:03:44,671 --> 00:03:48,641
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
